{
  "source": "Prompts/document-trap-2.mp4",
  "duration": 215.132875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.64,
      "text": "Your big season-end basketball tournament starts next week, so you definitely want to brush up on the rules."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.66,
      "end": 8.04,
      "text": "You upload your league's massive"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.46,
      "end": 14.9,
      "text": "200-page rulebook to an AI chatbot and ask a simple question. How many fouls until I'm out of the game?"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.76,
      "end": 20.36,
      "text": "Chat GBT answers instantly with total confidence, five fouls, and you foul out."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.9,
      "end": 27.86,
      "text": "Wait a second. In last year's tournament, you specifically remember a player picking up five fouls and staying on the court."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.5,
      "end": 35.54,
      "text": "You dig through the physical rulebook yourself to check. The regular season section says exactly what the AI did, five fouls."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.96,
      "end": 42.48,
      "text": "But buried near the back, there's a special section strictly for tournaments. In those games, players get six."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.36,
      "end": 50.2,
      "text": "The AI pulled the standard limit and missed the exception, delivering a factual but dangerously incomplete answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.98,
      "end": 56.66,
      "text": "This is the document trap. The assumption that an uploaded document is a fully understood document."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.46,
      "end": 66.82,
      "text": "Uploading a file doesn't mean the AI instantly memorizes every single word. A short file might fit entirely inside the AI's active memory, known as its context window."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.48,
      "end": 74.8,
      "text": "But when you ask a question about a long file, the system has to search the document and pull only the matching passages into that window."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.7,
      "end": 83.44,
      "text": "That highlights the flaw in the initial prompt. You were thinking about a tournament but failed to actually include the word tournament in your question."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.08,
      "end": 92.42,
      "text": "Because of that omission, the retrieval machine only pulled pages matching standard files. It left the AI completely blind to the tournament exception."
    },
    {
      "start": 93.34,
      "end": 103.38,
      "text": "To bypass this limitation, you need to formulate a revised prompt that gives the AI the exact context. You must explicitly ask for both the rule and the edge cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.12,
      "end": 110.44,
      "text": "Try asking it this way. In tournament games, how many fouls are allowed? Quote, the rule and any exceptions."
    },
    {
      "start": 111.32,
      "end": 119.22,
      "text": "Given that precise target, the AI's corrected answer now successfully acknowledges the explicit six foul allowance for leak tournaments."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.22,
      "end": 124.02,
      "text": "Since the AI only answers based on the text that reaches its context window,"
    },
    {
      "start": 124.54,
      "end": 129.48,
      "text": "explicit and specific prompting is the only reliable way to force it to retrieve the exceptions."
    },
    {
      "start": 130.58,
      "end": 135.04,
      "text": "This infographic outlines four tips for working with long documents. A"
    },
    {
      "start": 135.04,
      "end": 138.92,
      "text": "systematic approach to make the right passages easier for the retrieval machine to find."
    },
    {
      "start": 139.58,
      "end": 147.54,
      "text": "Step one, name the section. Using the documents exact headings and keywords creates a stronger magnet for the AI's search function."
    },
    {
      "start": 148.36,
      "end": 149.9,
      "text": "Step two, ask one thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.48,
      "end": 156.46,
      "text": "Multi-part questions confuse the retrieval target, giving the AI one clear question ensures higher accuracy."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.72,
      "end": 162.72,
      "text": "Step three, share what matters. Uploading a full 200-page file risks missing data,"
    },
    {
      "start": 162.72,
      "end": 165.6,
      "text": "pasting only the relevant section removes that risk."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.36,
      "end": 171.84,
      "text": "Finally, step four, ask for the quote. By asking the AI to quote the exact passage,"
    },
    {
      "start": 172.36,
      "end": 176.32,
      "text": "you can immediately compare its answer with the original text to verify the claim."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.28,
      "end": 185.38,
      "text": "These four moves will organize your evidence, but they do not guarantee a complete answer. Human vigilance remains your ultimate filter."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.28,
      "end": 189.42,
      "text": "The document trap extends far beyond the basketball court."
    },
    {
      "start": 189.86,
      "end": 193.44,
      "text": "Here in the real world, dense paperwork like apartment leases,"
    },
    {
      "start": 193.92,
      "end": 202.02,
      "text": "complex employment contracts, and financial aid letters routinely hide conditions or exceptions that can completely change your bottom line."
    },
    {
      "start": 202.88,
      "end": 211.12,
      "text": "Always remember, as this final board clearly states, uploaded doesn't mean fully read. Ask for the rule and any exceptions."
    }
  ],
